**Suggestion: Consider extracting marker injection to a separate method**

The debug marker injection code (lines 54-66) makes the main method harder to read. Consider extracting it:

```java
private void injectDebugMarker(Page page, int x, int y, String markerId) {
    page.evaluate("(args) => {\\n"
        + "  const [x, y, id] = args;\\n"
        + "  let dot = document.getElementById(id);\\n"
        // ... rest of the JavaScript
        + "}", new Object[] { x, y, markerId });
}

private void removeDebugMarker(Page page, String markerId) {
    page.evaluate("(id) => { const dot = document.getElementById(id); if (dot) dot.remove(); }", 
        new Object[] { markerId });
}
```

This would make the main execute method more readable and the debug logic more testable.

